  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "⛏️ Minecraft Username Generator",
      "tagline": "Usernames that fit Minecraft's rules, from GhastBuster to LostMyBed."
    },
    "intro": "This **Minecraft username generator** makes names that fit Minecraft's rules: 3 to 16 characters, using only letters, numbers and underscores. Choose a style, from mob and block names to cool, PvP, funny, cute and short OG-style names, and add numbers if the one you want is taken.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How long can a Minecraft username be?",
        "content": "<p>A Minecraft Java Edition username must be 3 to 16 characters long and can only use letters, numbers and underscores.</p><ul><li><strong>Length:</strong> on Java Edition a username must be 3 to 16 characters long.</li><li><strong>Characters:</strong> letters, numbers and underscores only. No spaces, dots or symbols, so <em>Ghast Buster</em> becomes <em>GhastBuster</em> or <em>Ghast_Buster</em>.</li><li><strong>Unique:</strong> every Java username is taken by one account only, so popular words go fast. Adding a number or an underscore is the usual way round it.</li><li><strong>Changing it:</strong> you can change your Java username once every 30 days, from your Minecraft profile.</li><li><strong>Bedrock Edition</strong> (consoles, phones, Windows) uses your Xbox gamertag instead, which has its own rules.</li></ul><p>Every name this generator makes fits the Java rules, so it'll work on either edition.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Cool, funny, PvP and OG Minecraft names",
        "content": "<p>The best Minecraft usernames are short, easy to spell out loud and say something about how you play.</p><ul><li><strong>Mob and block:</strong> names built from the game itself, like GhastBuster or CopperTamer.</li><li><strong>Cool:</strong> sharp two-part names like IronSpark or Onyx_Hawk.</li><li><strong>PvP:</strong> sweaty, competitive names for duels and Bedwars.</li><li><strong>Funny:</strong> names that admit what really happens, like LostMyBed or DirtLover.</li><li><strong>Cute:</strong> soft, friendly names that suit cosy builds.</li><li><strong>OG:</strong> short, rare-looking names in the style of early Minecraft accounts.</li></ul><p>None of the styles is just for boys or just for girls; pick whatever suits you. If you'd rather build a name from your own, try the <a href=\"minecraft-name-from-your-name.html\">Minecraft name from your name</a> generator. For other games, there's the <a href=\"gamertag-generator.html\">Gamertag Generator</a>.</p><p>For everything else in Minecraft, see all the <a href=\"../categories/minecraft-names.html\">Minecraft name generators</a>.</p><p>More for your Minecraft world: <a href=\"minecraft-server-name-generator.html\">server and SMP names</a>, <a href=\"minecraft-clan-name-generator.html\">clan and faction names</a> and <a href=\"minecraft-pet-name-generator.html\">pet names</a>.</p><p>Want a matching channel? The <a href=\"youtube-channel-name-generator.html\">YouTube Channel Name Generator</a> has names for Minecraft YouTube channels too.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How long can a Minecraft username be?",
        "answer": "On Java Edition, 3 to 16 characters, using only letters, numbers and underscores."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can a Minecraft name have spaces?",
        "answer": "No. Use capital letters (GhastBuster) or an underscore (Ghast_Buster) instead."
      },
      {
        "question": "How often can I change my Minecraft name?",
        "answer": "On Java Edition, once every 30 days. Bedrock Edition uses your Xbox gamertag, which you change through your Microsoft account."
      },
      {
        "question": "What should my Minecraft name be?",
        "answer": "Something short, easy to spell when a friend types it into a server, and not already taken. Pick a style, generate a few, and check the one you like is free on the Minecraft website."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are good Minecraft PvP names?",
        "answer": "Good Minecraft PvP names are short and sharp, like Onyx_Hawk or IronSpark. Choose the PvP style for sweaty, competitive names that look good in a kill feed."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are good OG Minecraft names?",
        "answer": "OG Minecraft names are short, three- or four-letter-looking names in the style of early accounts. Most real 3-letter names are taken, so the OG style makes short, rare-looking ones and you can add a number or underscore."
      }
    ]
  }
}
